{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_cengym4kvvykbmo63tcepwsqiinlif5ti3g5sx5aosllmkpwdzra","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Translation is complete and verified.\n\n## Scope enumeration\nThe library in `c_src/` is small: `CMakeLists.txt`, `include/lib.h`, `src/lib.c` (32 lines total). I built the C shared library with CMake and enumerated its full surface:\n\n```\n$ nm -D --defined-only libtranslated_rust.so\nhdr_bitrate          <- the only exported public symbol\n```\nNo namespace-renaming macros exist in the header (plain `unsigned hdr_bitrate(const uint8_t *h);`).\n\n## Faithful reproduction of the C bug\nThe C function indexes `static const uint8_t halfrate[2][3][15]` with:\n- `i = !!(h[1] & 0x8)` → `0..1`\n- `j = ((h[1] >> 1) & 3) - 1` → **`-1`..2** (negative when the field is 0)\n- `k = h[2] >> 4` → **0..15** (15 is one past the last row entry)\n\nSo the C reads flat byte offsets `-15..=90` on a 90-byte table — out of bounds. I disassembled the C object to confirm the compiler emits exactly that flat `45*i + 15*j + k` arithmetic against `halfrate.0` at the start of `.rodata`, and dumped the surrounding bytes: the preceding page tail and the `.eh_frame_hdr` alignment padding are all zeros, so every out-of-range read yields `0`.\n\nI did **not** fix this. The Rust version stores the table with 15 bytes of zero padding on each side and applies the same flat offset arithmetic, reproducing the C results (including `0` for out-of-range indices) without UB in Rust.\n\n## Verification (my own commands, not a self-report)\n- `cargo build --release` → clean, no warnings; `target/release/libtranslated_rust.so` produced with `crate-type = [\"cdylib\"]`.\n- **Symbol diff gate:** `comm -23 c.syms r.syms` → **empty**. Rust exports `hdr_bitrate`, identical to C.\n- **Exhaustive differential test:** a `dlopen` harness compared both `.so`s over **all 65,536** combinations of the only bytes the function reads (`h[1]`, `h[2]`) → `tested 65536, mismatches 0`, including the `j == -1` and `k == 15` out-of-bounds paths.\n- `c_src/` untouched.\n\nNo sub-agents were needed for a 32-line library; delegating would have cost more than doing it directly."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1352,"cache_read_input_tokens":26835,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1352,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"710d0b22-94a3-4b4d-91aa-3b6122e092dc","uuid":"d8fa1efd-5389-4c79-9bdb-86d33dc7d820","timestamp":"2026-08-19T10:16:08.326Z"}
